      "problem": "What is the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-125}-\\sqrt{32÷4+8}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, following the order of operations, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-125}-\\sqrt{32÷4+8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-125}-\\sqrt{8+8} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{-125}-\\sqrt{16} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-5)\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (-5)}-\\sqrt{4\\cdot 4} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-5)^{3}}-\\sqrt{{4}^{2}} & = \\\\ -5-4 & = \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
